@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# Windows enterprise CLI candidate
+
+Native Windows x64 AVX2 CLI/TUI, built on a Windows GitHub Actions runner. This
+profile requires NTFS, Windows installed at `C:\Windows`, Windows PowerShell 5.1,
+and administrator-managed `C:\Program Files\OpenCode Enterprise\enterprise.json`.
+Other system-drive layouts, ARM64, Desktop/Web and V2 are not supported by this
+candidate. Missing PowerShell or a rejected policy stops startup; there is no
+unmanaged fallback. The PowerShell ACL check is embedded in the binary and runs
+with a fixed executable path, no profiles, a minimal environment and a 10s limit.
+
+## Fresh installation
+
+1. Download `enterprise-windows-x64` from the successful Actions run. Verify the
+   outer artifact digest and the included `SHA256SUMS` against your approved
+   delivery record; public CI does not yet Authenticode-sign the executable.
+2. Extract the versioned Windows ZIP. Edit a copy of `enterprise.example.json`
+   with the approved internal gateway, one exact model and token limits. Never
+   put API keys into this policy. It is readable by local users.
+3. From an **administrator Windows PowerShell 5.1** console in the extracted
+   directory, run (use your actual policy path):
+
+   ```powershell
+   .\enterprise\windows\install.ps1 -PolicyPath C:\Staging\enterprise.json -BinaryPath .\opencode.exe
+   ```
+
+   The installer refuses to overwrite an existing installation. `-PolicyOnly`
+   installs just the protected configuration for disposable build runners or
+   managed provisioning before the binary exists. It does not validate inference.
+4. As a standard developer account, run:
+
+   ```powershell
+   & 'C:\Program Files\OpenCode Enterprise\opencode.exe' models
+   ```
+
+   Only `enterprise/<approved-model>` must appear. Perform actual inference,
+   streamed tool-call, cancellation, terminal and subagent acceptance checks.
+
+Owners must be SYSTEM, Administrators or TrustedInstaller. Non-administrators
+must not have write/delete/change-owner/change-ACL rights to the policy or its
+directory, or replacement rights on ancestors. Symlinks and junctions are
+rejected. The checker conservatively rejects unsafe allow ACEs even if another
+ACE denies them. Rights follow the Microsoft
+[FileSystemRights definitions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.security.accesscontrol.filesystemrights?view=netframework-4.8.1).
+The installer gives Users read/execute and Administrators/SYSTEM full control.
+
+## Deployment boundary
+
+Run as a standard user in a dedicated managed development VM/VDI. Do not give
+agent sessions local administrator rights. An administrator can replace both the
+binary and policy; application-level controls cannot protect against that.
+Require VPN identity, OS-enforced egress rules for **all child processes**, a
+router that forces one model, isolated workspaces and protected release delivery.
+Git for Windows is required for upstream shell/git workflows; provision it from
+an approved internal package source. Bash, Git, terminal/PTY and real vLLM flows
+need customer environment acceptance beyond `--version` / `models` CI checks.
+
+No automatic installation, driver, VPN, proxy, router, SSO or firewall provisioning
+is performed by this installer. Existing Linux deployment scripts remain Linux
+only. The platform design is documented in `delivery/DEPLOYMENT-ARCHITECTURE.md`
+in the public distribution repository / MVP toolkit.
+
+## Known release gates
+
+The previously reviewed inference timeout gap and saved-approval precedence risk
+remain unresolved by the Windows port. Native Windows standard-user acceptance,
+endpoint protection compatibility, actual VPN/gateway isolation, Authenticode
+signing, final dependency/image scan and signed private evaluation are required
+before production. CI tests synthetic ACL changes and policy failures using an
+administrator runner; that is not a complete workstation penetration test.
diff --git a/enterprise/windows/install.ps1 b/enterprise/windows/install.ps1
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5ae6f63
--- /dev/null
+++ b/enterprise/windows/install.ps1
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Run from an elevated Windows PowerShell 5.1 console. Fresh installations only.
+[CmdletBinding(DefaultParameterSetName="Install")]
+param([Parameter(Mandatory=$true)][string]$PolicyPath,
+      [Parameter(Mandatory=$true, ParameterSetName="Install")][string]$BinaryPath,
+      [Parameter(Mandatory=$true, ParameterSetName="PolicyOnly")][switch]$PolicyOnly)
+$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
+$target = 'C:\Program Files\OpenCode Enterprise'
+if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $target) { throw 'Installation already exists; use the managed update process' }
+$policy = [IO.File]::ReadAllText((Resolve-Path -LiteralPath $PolicyPath).Path)
+$binary = if (!$PolicyOnly) { (Resolve-Path -LiteralPath $BinaryPath).Path }
+# Protect the directory before placing either executable or configuration in it.
+[void][IO.Directory]::CreateDirectory($target)
+$acl = New-Object Security.AccessControl.DirectorySecurity
+$admin = New-Object Security.Principal.SecurityIdentifier('S-1-5-32-544')
+$acl.SetOwner($admin)
+$acl.SetAccessRuleProtection($true, $false)
+foreach ($sid in @('S-1-5-18', 'S-1-5-32-544', 'S-1-5-32-545')) {
+  $rights = if ($sid -eq 'S-1-5-32-545') { 'ReadAndExecute' } else { 'FullControl' }
+  $identity = New-Object Security.Principal.SecurityIdentifier($sid)
+  $rule = New-Object Security.AccessControl.FileSystemAccessRule($identity, $rights, 'ContainerInherit,ObjectInherit', 'None', 'Allow')
+  [void]$acl.AddAccessRule($rule)
+}
+[IO.Directory]::SetAccessControl($target, $acl)
+[IO.File]::WriteAllText("$target\enterprise.json", $policy, (New-Object Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))
+if (!$PolicyOnly) { [IO.File]::Copy($binary, "$target\opencode.exe", $false) }
+$files = if ($PolicyOnly) { @('enterprise.json') } else { @('enterprise.json', 'opencode.exe') }
+foreach ($name in $files) {
+  $fileAcl = [IO.File]::GetAccessControl("$target\$name")
+  $fileAcl.SetOwner($admin)
+  [IO.File]::SetAccessControl("$target\$name", $fileAcl)
+}
+if ($PolicyOnly) { return }
+& "$target\opencode.exe" --version
+if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Installed binary rejected policy; installation is not accepted' }
